※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4510

※ An exponent is how many times a value is multiplied by itself, which is a
※ count and therefore an integer.  A fractional power is a root, which no
※ instruction on any of these machines computes and which this language does
※ not offer; one is written as a call to whatever computes it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let x: f64 = 2.0f64 ⁿ 0.5f64
    0u8
